  "notes": [
    "fault moment = shear_modulus x potency (scalar moment for shear slip); the dike's muV comparison scale is reported by the distributed fits",
    "Okada surface displacements depend on the Lame constants only through alpha=(lambda+mu)/(lambda+2mu); uniformly rescaling (lambda, mu) changes no prediction and rescales the moments linearly, so the data do not constrain mu",
    "slip magnitudes remain regularized (positivity + smoothing at the reused smoothing weight); the sweep varies the depth cap on the fixed mapped trace and dip and gives conditional sensitivities, not a data-required depth or physical moment confidence bound",
    "truncation changes patch dimensions, Green's functions, and the retained smoothing operator; capped fits are not nested fits on one fixed basis, and saved capped fits can have slightly lower RMS than the uncapped fit",
    "a lower uniform shear modulus is an assumed sensitivity, not a stiffness inferred from these data; a depth-varying soft layer has not been modelled and would change the displacement calculation",
    "the graben band has a 6-km half-width from the dike axis and a 20-km along-axis half-length",
    "near-axis loop-closure inconsistencies reach 1-4 cycles (about 12-48 cm LOS); the check cannot identify the faulty leg or show that all flagged axial support was excluded from the model fits"
  ]
